LumOn - World-Probe Tracing and Surface Cache Lighting:

  Goal:
  Trace geometry independently of lighting readiness; resolve surface hits from the Surface Cache,
  distinguish sky from incomplete traces, and prevent unresolved work from starving publication.

  References:
  - docs/LumOn.SurfaceCache.LightingContract.md
  - docs/LumOn.TraceSceneGeometryContract.md
  - docs/LumOn.WorldProbeLighting.ArchitectureAndIssues.md

  Tasks:
  ✔ Diagnose the live Surface Cache readiness failure. Expose capture, direct-seed, and publication
    failure reasons; establish which condition prevents the first ready page before changing policy.
    - Diagnosed: prerequisite status and cumulative capture/seed/indirect/combine failure counters
      are exposed in runtime self-checks and periodic "[VGE] Surface cache readiness:" log entries.
      GPU rejection counters identify the failing operation, not the exact failing texel or input.
      Live run: all 24,948 captures failed; 38 pages awaited capture and no seed work started.
      Terrain feedback collapsed to slot 0. The terrain shader reads slot mapping from
      VgeLumonSceneChunkSlotParamsUBO, but its hook only uploaded obsolete standalone uniforms.
      Added the missing owned UBO and per-use binding restoration. The GPU regression maps to slot 232;
      removing only the new binding reproduces slot 0 with generation 0 while preserving the patch ID.
      Post-fix in-game publication remains to be verified under the live-validation task below.
  ✔ Correct temporal reprojection in lumon_velocity.fsh and lumon_debug_temporal.glsl: convert
    current render-relative positions into the previous render-origin space before projection.
    Validate translation, rotation, camera bob, and the dependent lumon_probe_atlas_temporal history.
    - Both renderers now pair committed view-projection matrices with their render origins and
      upload the previous matrix composed with the current-to-previous origin translation.
      Origin subtraction uses double precision; the full view transform retains camera bob.
    - Fresh build and all 29 focused tests passed: origin lifecycle and perspective (3), velocity
      translation/rotation/bob and invalid history (6), normal/debug renderer uploads (2), imported
      debug reprojection (1), and dependent probe-atlas temporal behavior (17). No tests skipped.
      In-game visual confirmation remains under the live-validation task below.
  ✔ Correct eye-relative view direction and distance in vge_parallax.glsl and vge_normaldepth.glsl.
    Account for the eye offset in the view matrix; validate parallax and normal-map fading with
    camera bob and camera offsets, without applying view translation twice.
    - Shared terrain view helper derives the eye from the existing draw's rigid modelViewMatrix.
      POM direction, POM distance fade, and normal-map distance fade use that same eye-relative
      vector. Surface positions remain render-relative and tangent frames remain in world axes.
    - Fresh build: 32 focused tests passed, including three imported GPU material regressions;
      one existing TinyTokenizer insertion test remains explicitly skipped. Verified shared
      vertex/fragment matrix linkage, rotation/bob offsets, POM displacement and normal fading.
      Full installed terrain variants and in-game visual behavior remain live-validation work.
  ✔ Make terrain PatchId and chunk-slot selection use the same inward-biased owning block in
    VanillaShaderPatches.cs and lumonscene_patchid.glsl. Validate all six faces at positive and
    negative chunk boundaries, including capture and sampling of the selected surface.
    - Patch mapping now returns its inward-biased absolute owning block. Terrain slot lookup uses
      that same block shifted by 5, preserving floor semantics at negative chunk boundaries.
      Patch-local integer layout arithmetic uses shifts for power-of-two scaling.
    - GPU regression executes the injected terrain mapping at all six faces on positive and negative
      chunk boundaries, with fractional camera motion and chunk crossings. Its actual slot/patch/UV
      feed voxel capture; sampling checks distinct materials on opposite sides of each boundary.
    - Fresh build: all 23 focused tests passed, none skipped. Restoring the old slot calculation
      inside the test failed all six positive-face boundary cases while eight controls passed.
      In-game visual confirmation remains under the live-validation task below.
  ✔ Remove vanilla GetLightRGBs and neighboring-light availability dependencies from world-probe
    geometry tracing when hit lighting is deferred to the Surface Cache.
    - Production workers disable vanilla sampling; geometry availability and legacy consumers retain
      their existing checks. Deferred sky scaling stays neutral for retained directional history.
    - All 55 focused tests passed, including actual GPU runtime publication with zero vanilla reads.
      Restoring the old dependency failed five regression cases, including 336 runtime light reads.
      In-game visual confirmation remains under the live-validation task below.
  ✔ Separate surface hits, established sky visibility, distance/budget exhaustion, and unavailable
    geometry. Define distant-light completion explicitly; do not turn incomplete traces into sky.
    - CPU outcomes now distinguish hit, sky, distance limit, traversal budget, unavailable data,
      and invalid input. Sky requires a clear route to the known upper world boundary; rays visit
      at most 512 cells. Signed-zero axis directions cannot select invalid DDA boundaries.
    - Incomplete primary rays retain their failure reason and retry without publishing samples.
      No independent distant-light provider exists yet; finite clear segments are not sky.
      Nearby occupancy accepts finite clearance; legacy secondary rays require established sky.
      Existing GPU CLEAR/BUDGET/unavailable semantics are preserved and documented.
    - Fresh build: all 133 focused CPU/GPU tests passed, none skipped. Coverage includes true sky
      exits, blocked/unloaded routes, finite and step limits, invalid rays, retry/publication and
      signed-zero directions. Short-range runtime traces publish neither radiance nor sky alpha;
      enclosed publication fixtures now have sufficient trace reach instead of relying on false sky.
      Restoring distance-limit-as-sky caused five expected failures, including GPU false lighting.
      In-game visual confirmation remains under the live-validation task below.
  ✔ Add Surface Cache indirect sky/distant-light completion using those outcomes. Reconcile it with
    the existing vanilla sunlight seed to avoid double-counting; retain retries for missing data.
    - Loaded upward rays complete at the authoritative integer world-top boundary, before reading
      geometry above it. Local coverage exits, unsupported/missing data and budget exhaustion retry.
    - Existing effective sunlight supplies direct sky/sun energy. Proven sky contributes zero
      additional indirect energy but counts in the full ray denominator and completed-batch weight.
      Surface hits still read previous outgoing radiance; world height is fixed for the loaded world.
    - The supported distant endpoint is the proven environment; no independent distant-surface
      provider or additional geometry coverage is introduced. Out-of-coverage rays remain unresolved.
    - Fresh shader build passed. All 12 environment tests passed after removing runtime world-height
      mutation assumptions; the 19 near-field/debug checks passed in the preceding verification.
      GPU evidence covers 256 texels across four complete sky-facing pages, a 128-ray mixed batch,
      both source policies, grazing coverage exits, unavailable inputs and preserved history.
      The preceding broader run passed 217 tests and failed 12; all 12 reproduced on isolated pristine HEAD,
      with one timing-sensitive doorway failure reproduced on its first isolated repeat.
      In-game visual confirmation remains under the live-validation task below.
  ✔ Preserve valid world-probe directional samples while retrying unresolved cache hits, with bounded
    work, per-direction validity, and generation-safe history so missing samples cannot publish light.
    - Ready cache answers publish independently; unresolved hit descriptors receive at most three
      additional GPU retries under the same admission ticket, then return to normal scheduling.
      Existing valid directions survive retry exhaustion. Queries remain bounded to 4096 hits and
      partial uploads share the configured byte budget. Primary geometry failures still reject
      their batch; they cannot be converted into sky or valid black.
    - Directional alpha zero remains invalid for direct and final-gather consumers. Valid black
      contact hits now encode a positive distance marker. Ring movement clears introduced slots
      while preserving overlapping probes; geometry dirtying, suppressed centers and dependency
      replacement retire affected history. Delayed answers must still match current tickets.
    - Regional invalidation now queues unique physical slots and clears them with one compute
      dispatch before atlas publication; full resets also use one dispatch. Overlapping regions
      cannot race or grow the queue beyond the allocated slot count. No per-region scissor or
      framebuffer-clear commands remain. A no-op flush dispatches nothing.
      Compute follow-up validation: 107 distinct GPU tests passed (104 regression tests plus
      three additional cases; final focused run 12/12), with no skips. Tests cover overlapping
      queue deduplication, empty flush, all four targets, wrapped slots, renderer early exits,
      shader-load rejection, and a 68,921-slot full reset across two dispatch dimensions.
      Shader build: 66 programs, 245 combinations. Subagent review found no remaining gap.
      Receipts: artifacts/TestResults/worldprobe-compute-clear.trx and
      artifacts/TestResults/worldprobe-compute-clear-final.trx. Live performance is unmeasured.
    - Validation: 148 distinct focused tests passed (147 regression tests plus one additional
      partial-upload budget test), with no skips; subagent review found no remaining production gap.
      Coverage includes mixed ready/unready/black answers, real subset retries, bounded work,
      direct/final-gather invalid samples, dirty-ticket rejection, wrapped slots, positive/negative
      anchor shifts, large moves, and existing cache/lifecycle/trace regressions. Shader validation
      built 65 programs across 244 combinations. Receipts: artifacts/TestResults/partial-worldprobe-final.trx
      and artifacts/TestResults/partial-worldprobe-subset-budget.trx. In-game validation remains open.
  ✔ Fix the confirmed initial-readiness blocker and prevent whole-page retry starvation, preserving
    valid progress without publishing uncaptured or uninitialized texels.
    - The diagnosed initial capture blocker was repaired by the terrain slot UBO binding above;
      all 14 terrain binding regressions pass again. No world-probe readiness or indirect-convergence
      dependency is required for the first valid direct seed to publish.
    - Seed buckets retain successful work and retry unresolved buckets. Partial seed pages alternate
      seed retries with indirect updates under the same page/texel/ray limits. Successful indirect
      texels publish even when other texels fail; failed ray batches preserve prior mean and weight.
    - Capture must finish coherently before lighting admission. Page readiness now admits some valid
      lighting; outgoing alpha independently rejects uninitialized texels. New identities reset direct,
      indirect and pending output before seeding. Full-tile combination writes either valid lighting
      or explicit unavailable zero, then bounded whole-tile carry-forward preserves both generations.
      Hidden faces retain an explicit direct-alpha marker so combination cannot add their emission.
      Reset, combine and copy each stay within a separate 65,536-texel ceiling; no atlas storage added.
    - Validation: 65 of 66 distinct tests passed, none skipped. The sole SH9 numerical failure exactly
      matches preserved pristine baseline (expected 1.2732395 +/- .08, actual 1.1865234).
      Coverage includes densities 1/4, mixed seed and indirect results, real GPU hit queries,
      incomplete capture, stale source history, hidden emission, scheduling, lifecycle and sky.
      Latest shader build: 66 programs / 245 combinations. Independent review found the hidden-face
      emission regression during development; it was corrected and covered, with no remaining gap.
      Receipts: artifacts/TestResults/surface-partial-page-final.trx and
      artifacts/TestResults/surface-partial-page-current.trx; prior baseline:
      artifacts/surface-sky-baseline-receipts/baseline.trx. Live validation remains below.
  Surface Cache refresh without global erasure:
  Evidence: docs/LumOn.SurfaceCache.ResetDiagnostics.md records the stationary dirty-chunk reset.
  ✔ Separate valid-but-stale lighting from invalid surface identity; update the lighting contract.
    - Preserve published lighting and unchanged captures after ordinary chunk/light notifications.
      Determine affected capture identities from relevant geometry/material changes; a dirty
      notification alone is not proof that every surface in the chunk changed.
    - Reject removed/replaced surfaces, reassigned pages, and delayed results with obsolete identities.
      Keep explicit initialization for new storage and hard invalidation for incompatible resources.
    - Implemented exact immutable sixteen-voxel capture identities, page content revisions and
      temporary source-availability gating. Unchanged/light-only notifications preserve captured
      material and lighting; changed patches alone recapture. Same-frame recapture cannot reuse
      prior lighting readiness. Scene/material and atlas lifetime changes retain hard initialization.
    - Source freshness no longer changes the cache dependency lifetime. LightingIsStale explicitly
      reports retained source-stale values. Pending GPU probe answers reject changed source
      invalidation revisions without globally erasing previously published probe directions.
    - Validation: 35 focused GPU/runtime tests passed; a final repeat also passed the strengthened
      capture-revision assertion. Coverage includes signed six-axis addressing, bounded identity
      storage, retained direct/indirect/outgoing data, suspended query rejection/recovery, selective
      same-chunk recapture, partial publication, hard replacement and delayed probe answers.
      Independent production review found no remaining identity-validity gap. Receipts:
      artifacts/TestResults/surface-identity-final.trx and
      artifacts/TestResults/surface-identity-capture-revision.trx.
      Normal mod build/deployment passed with zero warnings/errors; receipt:
      artifacts/surface-identity-deploy.log.
    - Direct-light freshness scheduling and temporal adaptation are tracked in the following tasks;
      retained old lighting is not a claim of updated-light convergence. In-game validation remains open.
  ✔ Replace global erase/recapture with bounded refresh scheduling for direct and indirect lighting.
    - Revisit already seeded pages for direct-light changes; keep successful partial work and fair
      retries. Geometry changes may affect lighting beyond the edited chunk: ensure all resident
      candidates receive eventual refresh without requiring a global clear or precise ray dependencies.
    - Continue serving the previous valid outgoing generation until replacement texels are ready;
      reconcile world-probe dependency tickets so stale work cannot republish an invalid surface.
    - Implemented recurring direct refresh alongside indirect tracing under one shared page budget.
      Published partial pages also retain seed-retry turns and successful initial bucket completion.
      Independent cyclic refresh buckets and identity-based page traversal preserve fairness through
      repeated dirty notifications and temporary eligibility loss, including resident pages outside
      the edited chunk. Unknown inputs retain prior values; confirmed exterior occupancy is rechecked.
    - Direct replacement preserves ordinary indirect history and the existing outgoing generation
      commit path. Refresh does not advance dependency lifetime or retire probe tickets; current
      geometry revision, admission ticket and cache lifetime guards still reject obsolete answers.
    - Validation: 39 focused tests passed, including direct on/off changes with unchanged capture,
      hidden/visible exterior transitions, unresolved refresh retention/recovery, repeated empty
      candidate rounds under a one-page budget, remote-chunk indirect sample progress, identity,
      partial-page publication, environment outcomes and delayed world-probe dependency rejection.
      Separate read-only implementation review found no remaining blocker. Receipt:
      artifacts/TestResults/surface-refresh-final.trx.
      Normal deployment passed with zero warnings/errors; 66 shader programs / 246 stage variants.
      Build receipt: artifacts/surface-refresh-deploy.log.
    - The following temporal task owns responsive indirect adaptation; the scheduling change left the
      running mean unchanged. These tests establish refresh work and direct replacement,
      not prompt indirect convergence or in-game acceptance.
  ✔ Make temporal accumulation responsive to changed lighting without clearing displayed results.
    - Define bounded history weighting/replacement for refreshes, preserving old valid values on
      unresolved attempts. Missing geometry, coverage exits and exhausted budgets remain unresolved.
      Do not publish uninitialized texels, false sky, or artificial black as successful refreshes.
    - Initially implemented an eight-completed-batch effective history cap: running mean during warm-up,
      then 1/8 replacement per successful sample. Higher existing weights migrate on the next
      completed finite sample without clearing RGB or changing publication identity. Fixed-input
      old-value contribution falls below 5% within 24 successful updates before storage rounding.
    - Unresolved attempts retain both RGB and weight. Nonfinite completed estimates are rejected
      before mutation. Proven sky and valid black remain resolved under the existing source policy.
      This is not a frame-time or multi-bounce convergence bound; no budget or storage was added.
    - Validation: 53 focused tests passed, including five new production-shader numerical cases
      for high-weight light-on/off response, warm-up/stability, failed-attempt retention, valid black,
      and real source removal without resetting indirect history. The remote-chunk regression now
      checks reduced indirect irradiance after a neighboring light edit rather than unbounded weight
      growth. Existing producer, environment, refresh, identity, partial publication, probe-ticket,
      capture-identity and scheduling coverage passed. Independent numerical/lifetime review found
      no blocker; receipt: artifacts/TestResults/surface-temporal-final.trx.
    - Normal production deployment passed with zero warnings/errors; receipt:
      artifacts/surface-temporal-deploy.log. Test compilation retained five pre-existing analyzer
      warnings in unrelated test files. In-game noise/response acceptance remains open.
    - Follow-up: RelightMaxFramesAccumulated is configurable (default 4, sanitized 1..255).
      Weighting now matches UE radiosity: alpha=1/(1+previousCount), followed by storing
      min(previousCount+1,limit). Default saturated new-sample weight is 1/5, not 1/4.
      Runtime limit changes preserve lighting and identity; the first resolved sample uses the
      previous count before storing the new cap. Default fixed-input residual is below 5% after
      14 saturated successful updates. Follow-up validation: all 66 focused tests passed, none skipped,
      including JSON/default/clamping, cap 1/4/8 GPU weighting, lower-cap and 1024-count migration,
      and live runtime configuration without capture/storage/dependency/readiness reset. Independent
      source review found no blocker. Receipt: artifacts/TestResults/surface-configurable-history.trx.
      Normal production build/deployment passed with zero warnings/errors; receipt:
