  Optional GPU tracing for L0 world probes:
  Scope: reuse existing uploaded local geometry; do not upload distant terrain for this backend.
  L1 and higher remain on the existing CPU tracer. Implement separately from Surface Cache refresh.
  ✔ Add an enabled-by-default GPU world-probe tracing feature flag and level-based backend routing.
    - Flag off: retain CPU tracing for every level. Flag on: route L0 to a separate GPU backend,
      leaving L1+ on the CPU. Share scheduling, admission tickets, direction selection and budgets.
    - Retire outstanding backend work safely on flag changes, world leave and resource replacement;
      prevent duplicate publication or stranded in-flight requests.
    - Implemented WorldProbeClipmap.EnableGpuTracing and separate L0 backend admission. The initial
      CPU compatibility adapter has now been replaced by the compute implementation below.
      Flag changes revoke pending tickets/queries without clearing displayed history. All 43
      focused tests passed; production build/deployment passed with zero warnings/errors.
      Routing, lifetime boundaries and evidence: docs/LumOn.WorldProbeGpuRouting.md.
  ✔ Implement bounded L0 compute tracing against the existing GPU geometry and Surface Cache.
    - Reuse GPU voxel traversal and surface-lighting lookup with integer world origins and local
      fractions. Preserve ray outcomes, directional distance encoding, confidence, short-range
      occlusion and importance metadata; geometry tracing must not require lighting readiness.
    - L0 placement does not guarantee full-ray coverage. Coverage exits and unsupported geometry
      require CPU fallback; missing lighting at a resolved hit remains a Surface Cache retry.
    - Implemented asynchronous batches of at most 8,192 rays, each bounded to 512 visited cells,
      integer origins and shared direction/metadata integration. Existing uploaded geometry is
      traced independently of lighting; ready hits bypass redundant cache queries. Explicit
      fallback outcomes now continue through the bounded CPU fallback described below.
      All 141 focused tests passed; production build/deployment passed with zero warnings/errors.
      Evidence and intermediate readback limits: docs/LumOn.WorldProbeGpuRouting.md.
  ✔ Use compact per-probe records, GPU-generated direction tiles and indirect trace dispatch.
    - Replaced repeated ray inputs with one 64-byte integer-origin probe and 4-byte selected
      texel indices. GPU setup builds 8-byte tile references and indirect arguments; 8x8 groups
      generate octahedral/cardinal directions and write separate 80-byte answers. Existing sparse
      direction scheduling and metadata remain shared. GPU-resident publication is described below.
    - All 143 regression tests plus 14 rebuilt admission/backend checks passed; production
      build/deployment passed with zero warnings/errors. See docs/LumOn.WorldProbeGpuRouting.md.
  ✔ Add bounded CPU fallback for L0 rays outside GPU coverage or unsupported by GPU geometry.
    - Retrace only fallback directions from their original probe origins using the existing CPU
      collision tracer. Merge results under the same admission identity without retracing or
      overwriting successful GPU directions. Keep fallback queues and work within explicit budgets.
    - Preserve unavailable, distance-limit and budget-exhaustion outcomes; never infer sky from
      leaving GPU coverage. If CPU fallback cannot resolve a ray, preserve history and retry.
    - Implemented one asynchronous collision-only worker, bounded to 64 outstanding admissions,
      8,192 retained answers and 256 CPU ray starts per frame (512 visited cells per ray).
      Retains GPU answers and original tickets; revalidates geometry/cache lifetimes before merge.
      CPU-confirmed unsupported hits can query captured lighting with existing readiness guards.
    - All 180 regression tests plus 12 rebuilt worker checks passed; production build/deployment
      passed with zero warnings/errors. Root review and independent test-agent audit found no
      blocker. Evidence and remaining runtime limitations: docs/LumOn.WorldProbeGpuRouting.md.
  ✔ Publish hybrid results through a coherent GPU completion and commit path.
    - Keep GPU directional payloads resident where practical; read back only bounded completion
