  Surface Cache tracing throughput:
  Scope: improve the Surface Cache producer independently of the completed L0 world-probe backend.
  Preserve valid displayed lighting, surface identity guards and partial progress throughout.
  ✔ Measure Surface Cache completion reasons and establish a matched baseline.
    - Add bounded aggregate counters for capture coverage/publication/material failures and indirect
      coverage exits, unavailable/unsupported geometry, traversal exhaustion and unready cache hits.
      Separate per-ray/texel outcomes from incomplete-page counts and report successful progress.
    - Measure capture, direct and indirect work, queue age, completion latency, GPU time and render
      thread/readback cost without verbose per-ray logging or new synchronous diagnostic readbacks.
    - Preserve the 2026-09-25 diagnostic baseline: recorded 4,657/5,006 pages awaiting capture,
      55,428/55,786 failed capture attempts and 11,683/11,822 incomplete indirect batches.
      These earlier gameplay counters do not identify individual failure reasons or current rates.
      All 20 focused diagnostic tests passed; receipt:
